				"integrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] Live-action, cinematic, 16:9 widescreen, a wide establishing shot of an ancient Jiangnan water town at golden hour — a grey stone arch bridge spans a calm river, willows trailing over the water, lanterns hanging from wooden eaves. Two girls in flowing Hanfu, one in soft pink and one in light blue, step onto the bridge and pause at the railing. The camera pushes in with small amplitude at slow speed, drawing closer to them.\n\n[Shot 2] At 00:03.500, the camera cuts to a medium two-shot of the two girls leaning together, hiding their smiles behind round silk fans as they gossip. The pink-robed girl (S1) says in a teasing whisper: <d>[Chinese] 你看，桥那头来了位公子，生得可真俊。</d> The blue-robed girl (S2) peeks over her fan and replies: <d>[Chinese] 当真？待我瞧瞧——果然风度翩翩！</d> The camera pushes in slightly as they giggle.\n\n[Shot 3] At 00:07.000, the camera cuts to a handsome young man in white robes walking toward them across the bridge, sleeves swaying in the breeze, a wooden sword at his waist, unaware of the attention. The camera tracks backward at slow speed, keeping him centered as the two girls blur in the foreground.\n\n[Shot 4] At 00:09.500, the camera cuts back to the girls, who drop their fans and glare at each other. S1 stamps her foot and says: <d>[Chinese] 是我先瞧见的，归我！</d> S2 steps forward and retorts: <d>[Chinese] 分明是我先！你休要抢！</d> The camera pushes in with small amplitude at fast speed as their voices rise.\n\n[Shot 5] At 00:12.500, the camera pulls out with large amplitude at fast speed as the two girls lunge at each other, grabbing sleeves and playfully tussling; fans fall to the stone bridge and one girl's hairpin slips loose. S1 cries: <d>[Chinese] 看招！</d> S2 squeals: <d>[Chinese] 哎哟！</d> The young man stops and turns back with a puzzled look as the shot ends on the chaotic, comic struggle.\n\noverall_soundscape: Gentle river water laps beneath the bridge while soft wind stirs the willow leaves, layered with distant tourist chatter and occasional birdsong. Silk fabric rustles as the girls whisper behind their fans, a fan snaps shut, then the tussle brings the slap of cloth, a light stumble of footsteps on stone, and stifled laughter.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: A playful Chinese instrumental piece with pipa and bamboo flute at a moderate tempo, light and sprightly during the gossip, quickening through the argument, and turning comic with staccato plucks as the fight breaks out, ending on a single final plucked chord.\n",
				1344,
				768,
				124
			],
